[#:seon.task{:name "check-reruns-on-request"
             :plan "`my.test/check` accepted `:seon.test/rerun?` (its request map is open) and dropped it: `my.test/check-now` built its `seon.test/run` request without it, so an agent could not force its recorded results to run again (astra day audit, interp-honest slice 4). Done when `:my.test/check-request` declares `:seon.test/rerun?` and `my.test/check` hands it to `seon.test/run`, so a named test recorded green executes again. Read `seon.test/select`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "run-answers-a-whole-namespace-without-a-verdict"
             :plan "(`my.test/run`) in seon.render.value-test ran all 52 members to test one new deftest: over 30 s, past MCP's default bound, which answered only a timeout with no handle (the run finished and recorded at 22:04:14). Its answer is a vector of 52 per-test maps in symbol order, so the shown text starts with green members and the one red test is cut. Answer passed?, counts and the red members first (`seon.test/tally`'s verdict) and accept a named test or the tests naming a task, as `my.test/check` does for changes. Read `my.test/run-owned` and `docs/research/agent-platform/repl-dogfood-2026-09-27.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "run-owned-reply-repeats-its-output"
             :plan "`my.test/run-owned` answers about 800 tokens for one test, with a duplicated :out. Done when the reply is focused through the render (one output, the verdict, the failing assertions' data) and its token size is asserted in a regression. Read `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/task-census/evidence/repl-audit--change.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "test-output-and-an-empty-reaching-run-reach-the-reply"
             :plan "A `my.test/check` reply carries clojure.test's \"Testing ns\" (and FAIL) lines in `:out`, printed outside the value printer; and the automatic test step reports `:seon.turn.loop/reaching {:seon.test/passed? false :seon.turn.loop/red []}` after an eval request on a fresh agent branch with no change (both observed on default 2026-10-08, agent integrate-2-probe). A one-test check there allocated 2.5 GB in 1.67 s. Done when the report reaches the agent only as data and a reaching run with nothing to run says so instead of `passed? false`. (The pilot's other half, a test named as changed being refused, no longer reproduces.). Read `seon.test/run`, `seon.turn/run-reaching` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-08/dogfood/pilot.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "check-ignores-the-tests-key"
             :plan "(my.test/check {:seon.test/tests [sym]}) ignores the key and runs the tests reaching the named function instead (13 s) (default, 2026-10-08). Done when a named test list runs exactly those tests, with a regression, or the request schema refuses the key. Read `my.test/check`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-agent-cannot-run-one-test-by-hand"
             :plan "At an agent's REPL (clojure.test/run-test-var #'t) throws ClassCastException (sci.lang.Namespace cannot be cast to clojure.lang.Symbol), (clojure.test/run-test t) and (clojure.test/test-vars [#'t]) answer nil, and calling the deftest prints FAIL lines located at (lookup.clj:43) (fanout run, default e1a71b7c8, 2026-10-08; agents fan-source and live-flash-4 tried these). Done when clojure.test's own run-test-var and run-test answer their summary map at the agent's REPL, as in Clojure. Reproduced again on default caba650fa (agent chain-frictions-probe, 2026-10-10): (ns cf.scratch (:require [clojure.test :as t])) (t/deftest cf-t (t/is true)) (t/run-test-var #'cf-t) throws \"class sci.lang.Namespace cannot be cast to class clojure.lang.Symbol\" (1 ms). Same class as `seon.sci.eval` task run-test-var-throws-on-an-sci-test-var, whose proof this task shares. Read `my.test/run-owned`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-two-test-check-allocates-a-gigabyte-and-a-half"
             :plan "(`my.test/check` {:seon.test/changed ['seon.db/registered-attribute-candidates 'seon.db/missing-connection-error]}) at root ran two reaching tests whose run-ms were 40 and 22 ms but took 1,395 ms and allocated 1,419 MB (fanout-3 run, default 324461975, 2026-10-09); a check reaching nothing (my.test/check-now) took 186 ms and 311 MB. Done when a check's cost follows the tests it runs, its allocation owners named by `seon.profile/measure`. Read `seon.test/run`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-check-failure-shows-no-message"
             :plan "`my.test/check` rendered an errored test as only `{:seon.test/sym ...}` under `:seon.render.test/failures` (2026-10-09); its message, \"The admitted identity has no executable test Var.\", was found three evaluations later under `:seon.test/results` `:seon.test.failure/reports`. Done when each listed failure shows its report message."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-green-check-answers-no-per-test-counts"
             :plan "`my.test/check` of 17 named tests (agent eval-fixes-3, default a740b1e26, 2026-10-10, run f11a3891e603) answered `:seon.test/passed? true` and `:seon.test/executed-count 17` with `:seon.test/results` empty: the pass, fail and error count of each test was readable only by querying the run's `:seon.test.run/members` and each `:seon.test.member/pass-count`. Done when the answer carries each executed test's counts by symbol. Read `seon.test/run`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "an-agent-call-reaches-resolve-test-without-its-class-loader"
             :plan "An agent's evaluation reached `seon.test/resolve-test` without `:seon.test/class-loader`, and the contract refused it (`:seon.test/resolution-request`): agent ap-probe-2 on default 340462543, branch :agent-9996d823c28d, 2026-10-10 11:54:55, recorded as an agent error with signature 4e3dc9667cd3. Its request was `(require 'seon.competency-test)`, a `my.test/check` naming `seon.competency-test/t5-slug-removes-edge-hyphens` as changed, then `seon.test/reaching` and a `seon.db/pull`. The caller building the resolution request from an agent's world omits the class loader the request requires. Done when that caller supplies it, or the request's schema says why an interpreted resolution needs none, with a regression running the same forms as an own-branch agent that records no error. Read `seon.test/run`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-check-of-named-identities-answers-a-reused-reds-failure-reports"
             :plan "(chain 4 and chain 2, G12; met twice) `(my.test/check {:seon.test/identities #{sym}})` of a test whose recorded result is red answers `{:seon.test/passed? false}` and nothing else, while the same test named by `:seon.test/changed` answers its results and failure reports. `my.test/check` must answer the same `:seon.test/results` (with `:seon.test.failure/reports`) for a reused red as for a run one; the producer is the reuse branch of `seon.test/run` reached from `my.test/check`. Red proof: `my.test-check-test/a-check-of-named-identities-answers-a-reused-reds-failure-reports`. See also `my.test/a-check-failure-shows-no-message` and `seon.turn/a-red-proof-carries-no-reason`, which concern the render of a run's failures. Read `seon.render.test/render-ai` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-12/chain-experiment-4.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-defn-request-runs-four-tests-for-seven-gigabytes"
             :plan "A `defn` of `seon.sci.forgive/scan` on an agent's branch (2026-10-14) answered `:seon.turn.loop/tests {:reaching {:seon.test/passed? true :red []}}` with `:tests {:alloc-mb 222.5 :ms 196.0 :count 4}` but `:stages {:test-step 5745.2}` and `:step {:alloc-mb 7268.5}`; the first `defn` of the same function: `:test-step 2140.8`, `:step :alloc-mb 2614.0`, four tests. The tests account for 3% of the test step's allocation. Find the 7 GB (reach selection? derive? the result record?) and fix it at its producer. Measured (lane teststep-verdict, default 5fddc2bfd, 2026-10-14, a two-function scratch namespace with two 20 ms tests): test-step 0.8-1.1 s and 1.0-1.3 GB per `defn` of an existing function, 3.8-4.8 s and 5.7-7.1 GB on the request that first defines the namespace's tests; profile-cell deltas (JVM-wide, other lanes' work excluded by tree) inside `seon.test/run` (826-935 ms): `seon.test/changed-definition-symbols` 381-390 ms (under `seon.test/select`, 396-407 ms: `db/since` over the branch history), `seon.test.runner/commit-results!` 187 ms, `seon.test/clean-request-handle` 157 ms, `seon.test/member-result` 126 ms (`seon.test.runner/reach-memberships`/`reach-graph`); the same two tests run by `my.test/check` without a change cost 345 ms and 232 MB. Proof: a `seon.profile/measure` assertion on the request. Read `my.test/run-owned` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-14/repl-trial.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "the-reaching-verdict-of-a-defn-reply-omits-a-red-task-proof"
             :plan "Root cause (lane teststep-verdict, 2026-10-14): `seon.turn/run-reaching` runs `seon.test/reaching`, the nearest-test walk (`seon.fn/closure-walk` at depth 2), which stops at the first caller level holding a test, so a task's proof reaching the change through a helper one level further is never run and the reply's `:seon.turn.loop/reaching` answers `passed? true`; the full closure (`seon.fn/reverse-closure`) of `seon.sci.forgive/scan` is 642 tests (44 ms), of which 3 prove a `seon.sci.forgive` task, `forgiving-forgiven-text-changes-nothing` among them. Fix (patch `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-14/teststep-verdict-task-proofs.patch`, `src/seon/turn.clj` held by lane proj-content-key): the step's reaching request also names the tests carrying a task of a changed function's namespace that reach it at any depth. Red proof: `seon.turn.test-step-verdict-test/the-step-runs-a-task-proof-that-reaches-the-change-past-the-nearest-tests`. After the first `defn` of `seon.sci.forgive/scan` the reply said `{:seon.turn.loop/reaching {:seon.test/passed? true, :seon.turn.loop/red []}}`, yet `(my.test/run-owned {:seon.ns/name 'seon.sci.forgive-test})` in the next request answered `seon.sci.forgive-test/forgiving-forgiven-text-changes-nothing` with `:seon.test/fail-count 1` (it carries the open task `seon.sci.forgive/forgiving-forgiven-text-changes-nothing` in `:seon/tasks` and reaches `seon.sci.forgive/scan`): the defn reply ran 4 of the 15 tests of the namespace. A task's tagged proofs that reach the changed definition belong in the reaching selection, or the reply says which reaching tests it did not run. Read `my.test/run-owned` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-14/repl-trial.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-test-var-run-in-the-defining-request-answers-the-previous-red"
             :plan "Root cause (lane teststep-verdict, 2026-10-14): an eval request records its definitions in ONE transaction after its last form, so a later form's test run (`seon.sci.lookup` `agent-test-vars` -> `my.test/check` -> `seon.test/run`) selects, digests reach and acquires its world from the branch head without the request's own definitions: it reuses the record of the previous definition (`:seon.test/unchanged true`), and with `:seon.test/rerun? true` it executes the head's program (green for a definition the agent just replaced), records that, and the next `defn` Var render shows a false `:seon.render.var/newly-green`. Needs a design decision on the one REPL path (options in the lane's report: the evaluation's pending definitions as a `d/with` database the later forms read, or a test run in the defining request answered by the request's own test step). Red proof: `seon.turn.test-step-verdict-test/a-test-run-in-the-request-that-redefined-its-callee-answers-the-new-definition`. In one `eval_clj` request, `(defn- scan ...)` followed by `(clojure.test/test-vars [#'seon.sci.forgive-test/a-stray-closer-between-tokens-names-both-changes])` answered the record of the run before the `defn` (`:seon.test/unchanged true`, `:seon.test/run-basis-t` older than the definition, `:seon.test/fail-count 1`) while the request's own reaching step reported the same test green. A test run inside the request that changes its reach must derive the reach after the form. Read `my.test/run-owned` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-14/repl-trial.md`."}]
